<% html_title 'Performance', 'Periodic Returns' %>
<% content_for :header_tags do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'performance', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey' %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_owner_picker', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_navigation', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag 'performance_leaderboard', plugin: 'redmine_ticket_journey', defer: true %>
<% end %>
<div class="performance-page periodic-page periodic-returns">
  <%= render 'header', page_title: 'Periodic Performance — Returns' %>
  <p class="periodic-provisional"><strong>Returns calculation rules have been confirmed.</strong> Expected Done Tickets match Periodic Tickets' Completed from Expectation. Return counts use full recorded history through RED, including earlier incidents. Trends group these tickets by completion period. <a href="#periodic-return-rules">Read the rules</a>.</p>
  <p class="performance-context">Current Ticket Owner · Visible project hierarchy and tickets · Same tracker scope and current-status exclusions as Periodic Tickets · Metric includes Merge Conflict</p>
  <% if @periodic_return_report %>
    <% result = @periodic_return_report; total = result[:total] %>
    <p><strong><%= @owner_label %></strong><% if @selected_owners.any? { |owner| !owner.active? } %> · Includes inactive owners from saved selections; picker lists active users only.<% end %></p>
    <section class="performance-section periodic-summary">
      <h3><%= @selected_owners.size > 1 ? 'Owner Comparison and Team Results' : 'Return Quality Summary' %></h3>
      <% [:expected, :total].each do |population| %>
        <details><summary>Show <%= population == :expected ? 'Expected Done' : 'Total Done (Expected + Other)' %> results by owner and team</summary>
          <%= render 'periodic_return_comparison', population: population %>
        </details>
      <% end %>
      <details><summary>Show return distributions by owner</summary>
        <div class="autoscroll"><table class="list"><thead><tr><th>Owner</th><th>Expected Done</th><% ['0', '1', '2', '3', '3+ (≥4)', '1 repeat', '2 repeats', '2+ repeats (≥3)'].each do |label| %><th><%= label %></th><% end %></tr></thead><tbody>
          <% (@periodic_return_owners + [{ owner: nil, report: result }]).each do |entry| %><% ids = entry[:owner] ? [entry[:owner].id.to_s] : @selected_owner_ids; report = entry[:report][:expected] %>
            <tr class="<%= 'periodic-total-row' unless entry[:owner] %>"><th><%= entry[:owner]&.name || 'Team total' %></th><td><%= performance_return_link(report[:population], 'returns_open', ids) %></td>
              <% %w[returns_0 returns_1 returns_2 returns_3 returns_4 repeats_1 repeats_2 repeats_3].each do |key| %><td><%= performance_return_link(report[:sets][key].size, key, ids) %></td><% end %>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody></table></div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Expected Done Tickets — Return Quality</h3>
      <div class="periodic-return-kpis">
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Expected Done Tickets</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(@returns[:population], 'returns_open') %></strong><p>Completed from Expectation</p></article>
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Total Return Incidents</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(@returns[:incidents], 'return_incidents') %></strong><p>Incidents, not ticket count</p></article>
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Tickets with ≥1 Return</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(@returns[:returned], 'return_incidents') %></strong><p><%= @returns[:population].zero? ? 'N/A — no Expected Done Tickets' : "#{performance_number(@returns[:returned] * 100.0 / @returns[:population])}% of Expected Done Tickets" %></p></article>
        <article class="performance-metric performance-return-metric"><h4>Return Ticket Metric</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(performance_number(@returns[:ratio]), 'return_incidents') %></strong><p>Incidents / tickets with ≥1 return</p><p><%= performance_return_metric_note(@returns) %></p></article>
      </div>
      <p>Within <%= @returns[:population] %> Expected Done Tickets, <%= @returns[:returned] %> have at least one return, contributing <%= @returns[:incidents] %> incidents. The primary metric is a number, not a percentage.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Non-Merge Return Metrics</h3>
      <div class="performance-return-ratios">
        <%= render 'return_non_merge_metric', report: @returns, title: 'Expected Done — Non-Merge Incidents per Returned Ticket', numerator_metric: 'non_merge_incidents', denominator_metric: 'non_merge_denominator', unknown_metric: 'unknown_return_reasons' %>
        <%= render 'return_non_merge_metric', report: total, title: 'Total Done — Non-Merge Incidents per Returned Ticket', numerator_metric: 'total_non_merge_incidents', denominator_metric: 'total_non_merge_denominator', unknown_metric: 'total_unknown_return_reasons' %>
      </div>
      <p>Both denominators retain tickets with merge-only returns. Values are incident averages, not percentages. A known zero numerator gives 0 with a nonzero denominator; missing reasons remain unavailable.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="performance-return-distributions">
      <%= render 'return_distribution', number: 1, title: 'Return Count Distribution (Expected Done Tickets)', keys: %w[returns_0 returns_1 returns_2 returns_3 returns_4], labels: ['0 Return', '1 Return', '2 Returns', '3 Returns', '3+ Returns'], denominator: @returns[:population], total_metric: 'returns_open', total_label: 'Expected Done Tickets' %>
      <%= render 'return_distribution', number: 2, title: 'Consecutive Return Distribution (Expected Done Tickets)', keys: %w[repeats_1 repeats_2 repeats_3], labels: ['1 Consecutive Return', '2 Consecutive Returns', '2+ Consecutive Returns'], denominator: @returns[:with_repeats], total_metric: 'repeats_all', total_label: 'Tickets with Consecutive Returns' %>
    </div>

    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Return Metric — Total Done Tickets (Expected + Other)</h3>
      <div class="periodic-return-kpis">
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Total Done Tickets</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(total[:population], 'total_open') %></strong></article>
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Return Incidents</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(total[:incidents], 'total_return_incidents') %></strong></article>
        <article class="performance-metric"><h4>Tickets with ≥1 Return</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(total[:returned], 'total_return_incidents') %></strong></article>
        <article class="performance-metric performance-return-metric"><h4>Incidents / Returned Ticket</h4><strong><%= performance_return_link(performance_number(total[:ratio]), 'total_return_incidents') %></strong><p><%= performance_return_metric_note(total) %></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <% if @selected_owners.size > 1 %>
      <section class="performance-section"><h3>Return Ticket Metric by Owner</h3>
        <p>Expected Done Tickets · Incidents per returned ticket · Lower is better · Owners are listed alphabetically, without ranks.</p>
        <% maximum = [@periodic_return_owners.map { |entry| entry[:report][:expected][:ratio].to_f }.max.to_f, 1.0].max %>
        <% @periodic_return_owners.each do |entry| %><% report = entry[:report][:expected] %>
          <div class="periodic-bar-row"><span><%= entry[:owner].name %></span><div class="periodic-bar-track"><%= performance_return_link(content_tag(:span, '', class: 'periodic-bar-fill periodic-return-bar', style: "width:#{report[:ratio].to_f * 100 / maximum}%;"), 'return_incidents', [entry[:owner].id.to_s], 'aria-label': "#{entry[:owner].name}: #{performance_number(report[:ratio])} incidents per returned ticket") %></div><b><%= performance_return_link(performance_number(report[:ratio]), 'return_incidents', [entry[:owner].id.to_s]) %></b></div>
        <% end %>
        <p>Team metric: <strong><%= performance_number(@returns[:ratio]) %></strong> = <%= @returns[:incidents] %> incidents / <%= @returns[:returned] %> returned tickets. This is not an average of owner metrics.</p>
      </section>
    <% end %>
    <%= render 'periodic_return_trend', metric_key: :ratio %>
    <%= render 'periodic_return_trend', metric_key: :adjusted_ratio %>
    <section class="performance-section"><h3>Population and Data Quality</h3>
      <p>Expected Done Tickets must match the <%= periodic_ticket_link('Completed from Expectation', 'completed') %> list on Tickets. Total Done must match <%= periodic_ticket_link('Total Actual Done', 'actual') %>.</p>
      <p><%= periodic_ticket_link("Done tickets without recorded completion dates: #{@periodic_report[:sets]['missing_completion'].size}", 'missing_completion') %> · These do not increase delivered work or Returns denominators.</p>
      <p><%= periodic_ticket_link("Tickets excluded by current status: #{@periodic_report[:sets]['excluded'].size}", 'excluded') %> · <%= periodic_ticket_link("Extraordinary tickets: #{@periodic_report[:sets]['extraordinary'].size}", 'extraordinary') %></p>
      <p><%= periodic_ticket_link("Archived or On-Hold during period: #{@periodic_report[:sets]['archived_on_hold_period'].size}", 'archived_on_hold_period') %></p>
      <p>Missing/hidden return reasons do not remove incidents from the primary metric. Audits show unavailable reasons without exposing hidden data. All returns through RED count, including those before RSD.</p>
    </section>
  <% else %><p class="nodata">Select Ticket Owner(s) and the reporting period, then click Apply. No tickets or return histories have been scanned.</p><% end %>
  <details class="performance-notes" id="periodic-return-rules"><summary>Returns calculation rules</summary>
    <p>The Returns definitions have been confirmed. Part 1 rules define expectation, current owner, due dates and status checks. Delivery requires Done at RED and now; current excluded statuses are removed. Expected Done and Total Done reuse those exact sets.</p>
    <p>Qualifying transitions into Returned use existing tracker/stage rules. Count full recorded history through RED, including before RSD, with Merge Conflict included. Progress, completion and reassignment never reset return totals. Native lifetime Return Count is unchanged.</p>
    <p><%= performance_consecutive_returns_definition %> The consecutive-distribution denominator is only tickets with at least one consecutive repeat, not every returned ticket. “3+” means ≥4 returns; “2+” means ≥3 repeats.</p>
    <p>Metric = incidents / tickets with ≥1 return. A zero denominator is N/A (not applicable) with an explicit empty/no-return explanation; zero incidents are still shown. Team ratios use combined counts. The non-Merge metric uses the same returned-ticket denominator, excluding merge incidents only from its numerator. Missing reason data makes that metric unavailable. A known zero non-merge numerator with returned tickets gives 0.</p>
    <p>Weekly completion cohorts (monthly for periods over 120 days) partition Expected Done from the final RED package. Each ticket's latest qualifying completion determines its cohort; return counts still run through RED. Trends are not cumulative and do not rebuild expectation separately each week. Cohort counts sum to the main result; cohort ratios must not be averaged to get the overall metric.</p>
    <p>Metric changes to Live use returned open tickets as denominator while retaining its open scope and five month-end snapshots. The non-Merge metric uses the same incident-average units and returned-ticket denominator on Live and Periodic populations. Consecutive returns on Live use open tickets at the selected date; Periodic uses completed expected tickets as a lagging comparison.</p>
  </details>
</div>
